# Multi-project workspace layout

## Directories

- **`apps/`** — Deployable applications (web, API, workers, mobile shells). One subdirectory per app (e.g. `apps/web`, `apps/api`).
- **`packages/`** — Shared libraries (domain types, clients, UI kit, validation). Prefer small, focused packages over one catch-all unless the stack dictates otherwise.

## Conventions

- **New service or app**: add under `apps/<name>` with its own build/tooling as needed.
- **Shared code used by more than one app**: extract to `packages/<name>`.
- **Root** — Workspace-level config only (workspace file, CI, tooling that applies to everything). Avoid app logic at the repository root.

If the tech stack is not chosen yet, keep placeholders until the first app is scaffolded; do not invent framework-specific files preemptively.
